      "position": 0,
      "content": "GENERAL information",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "d2ed7145-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "This agreement is subject to revision without prior notice. Please check with a counselor every semester to obtain current information about possible changes in the agreement. To learn more about the courses and programs offered at Sonoma State University or the General Education and Upper-division requirements for each major please refer to the university catalog at: http://www.sonoma.edu/catalog/",
      "contentHtml": "This agreement is subject to revision without prior notice.  Please check with a counselor every semester to obtain current information about possible changes in the agreement.  To learn more about the courses and programs offered at Sonoma State University or the General Education and Upper-division requirements for each major please refer to the university catalog at: <a href=\"http://www.sonoma.edu/catalog/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sonoma.edu/catalog/</a>"
    },
    {
      "id": "3cf87845-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "important transfer information",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "86207745-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "Students must earn a minimum grade of C- or better in each of the six required courses for the major. Majors may apply up to 8 units of lower division coursework towards the requirements. Of these 8 units, no more than 4 units may be non-SSU transfer credit. Any lower division units used to meet the major&#39;s statistics requirement will not be included in either of these limits.",
      "contentHtml": "Students must earn a minimum grade of C- or better in each of the six required courses for the major.\r\n                                                                                \r\nMajors may apply up to 8 units of lower division coursework towards the requirements.  Of these 8 units, no more than 4 units may be non-SSU transfer credit.  Any lower division units used to meet the major&#39;s statistics requirement will not be included in either of these limits.\r\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "831e7745-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "Associate degree for transfer information",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0eec6545-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 5,
      "content": "The AA-T in Sociology (SB 1440 degree) has been deemed a \"similar\" degree to the Sociology, B.A. at Sonoma State. Students transferring to SSU with an AA-T in Sociology are advised to complete all available articulated major requirement and support courses before transfer. It is also recommended that students complete the American Institutions (US-1, US-2, US-3), and Seawolf Studies Graduation requirements before transfer.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>The AA-T in Sociology (SB 1440 degree) has been deemed a \"similar\" degree to the Sociology, B.A. at Sonoma State. Students transferring to SSU with an AA-T in Sociology are advised to complete all available articulated major requirement and support courses before transfer. It is also recommended that students complete the American Institutions (US-1, US-2, US-3), and Seawolf Studies Graduation requirements before transfer.</p>"
    }
